e general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(11t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(11t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -11 \\\\ 11 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*"] ["question-bf38a5cc-97dd-5fd2-8a65-012c6037d3ea" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -11 \\\\ 11 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -11 \\\\ 11 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(11t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(11t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(11t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(11t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(11t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(11t)\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"] ["question-bf38a5cc-97dd-5fd2-8a65-012c6037d3ea" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-79936db0-1d3e-5e44-88a9-d11010029275" :answer-field/id #uuid "79936db0-1d3e-5e44-88a9-d11010029275"] ["answer-8e4da7fb-aa00-5923-b65b-fbadd3556bb1" :answer/id #uuid "8e4da7fb-aa